<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center" class="tborder" style="border-bottom: 0;">
	<tr class="titlebg">
		<td valign="middle" align="left" width="15%" style="padding-left: 6px;">
			<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/topic/veryhot_post.gif" alt="" />
			Author
		</td>
		<td valign="middle" align="left" width="85%" style="padding-left: 6px;">
			Topic: Good guild going bad &nbsp;(Read 4279 times)
		</td>
	</tr>
</table>
<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="bordercolor">
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=511" title="View the profile of hegemony">hegemony</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Jackass<br />
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 1<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								An Everquest Player on Rodcet Nife<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=511"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=751.msg6665#msg6665"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=751.msg6665#msg6665">Good guild going bad</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b> on:</b> April 05, 2004, 04:20:29 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							First i would like to apologize to everyone at the Fennin Ro raid last night. During the fight at the beginning i was #4 in the CHR. FR i believe got too close to me and i was hit with his AE. When i realized that i had been hit i was around 20%. I then panicked and without thinking used my Purify AA (which cures any dot etc) and fast healed myself to prevent from dieing. While i was curing/healing myself i had to call skip in the CHR because i was casting. That is where i made my mistake and knew it right after i did it. Me calling skip caused Figgil to die and caused the Raid to almost wipe. The fight shouldn&#039;t have been as hard and sloppy as it was. And i&#039;d like to say sorry for my mistake. <br /><br />After FR died i was immediately sent a tell by a officer yelling at me and asking me why i skipped. After the discussion i was threatened to be removed from the guild if i did it again. I was also contacted by another officer later on in the night with the same message of removal if it happened again. The officer also informed me that this was my second skip and that the other was on a Xegony raid. I remembered that I called skip on Xegony because the MT (forgot who it was) ran OOR of me so i called skip even though i tried to cast CH on him several times. <br /><br />This upsets me that i get threatened of guild removal after an error on a raid. I thought Hegemony was a Family guild? This sounds like something FoT, Forsaken, Ascent etc do when someone messes up. I have been in this guild for 2 years. Lets remember Everquest is a game, don&#039;t hurt people&#039;s feelings and get upset over a game. I have a 70% RA for the last 3 months. I raid almost every single day with this guild and give my best everyday. Again I am sorry i messed up. If you want me to answer anymore questions send me a tell ingame. <br />_________________<br />&nbsp; <br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />tylerborne<br />Guild Member<br />&nbsp;<br />65 Human Cleric<br />Joined: 14 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 127<br /><br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 12:57 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />Hegemony is a raiding guild. Has been for 6 months now. I&#039;ve asked apps be turned away for less then stellar performances. But I will give you kudos for stepping up and letting everyone know your side. <br />_________________<br />Tylerborne <br />Archon of Hegemony <br /><br />Tylerborne <br />Dedluv &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Desai<br />Guild Member<br />&nbsp;<br />65 High Elf Cleric<br />Joined: 15 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 134<br />Location: Des Moines<br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 1:02 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />To me each situation needs to be evaluated and a decision needs to be made. I can understnad the importance of &#039;no skip&#039;, but on the other hand a dead cleric does no one any good. <br /><br />It&#039;s a hard call, you did what you though needed to be done at the time. I wonder if others do things like you did, but just don&#039;t call it. At least you let it be known what was going on. <br />_________________<br />&nbsp;<br />Desai Madidad <br />&lt;Hegemony&gt; <br />65 Cleric <br />Rodcet Nife &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />zaphe<br />Guild Member<br /><br />65 Iksar Shaman<br />Joined: 13 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 49<br /><br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 1:04 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />WHOEVER gave you a *removal from guild* talk because yo ucalled skip is an asshole and should be removed themselves. I may not be an officer but I&#039;m a member, which is JUST AS IMPORTANT. <br /><br />I won&#039;t tolerate crap like that coming from autority figures . thowing your weight around threatening members becuase of a mistake or an action thought to be right at the time. <br /><br />If anyone wants to talk you can PM me or just hash it out right here .. but I personally won&#039;t stand for ANYONE to be degraded like that. <br /><br />EDIT: I may not be one of the oldest members of Hegemony, but I have been around a while and I&#039;m not scared to stick up for fellow members who are being treated injustly. It seems that many don&#039;t wish to stick their head out of the sand to stick up for our teammates .. thats not me. <br />_________________<br />Zaphe Vo`Lok <br />65 Prophet of Cazic-Thule <br />No longer Shaman Class Leader <br />Hegemony, Rodcet Nife Server &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Oneiron<br />Guild Member<br /><br />64 Half Elf Druid<br />Joined: 16 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 2<br /><br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 1:23 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />I guess having the log in server inaccessable is not necessarily a good thing for me. I took some time to review the posts and, after getting to this thread, feel it is time I spoke up some. <br /><br />I am a long time full member - I can still remember the first time we were all abuzz because a /who all Hegemony was cut short when there were too many peeps on to list. However, things have changed...the guild is not what it used to be and this saddens me. It saddens me to see such responses as this one and the ones in the backflagging thread. I don&#039;t really care what the guild goal is, the reason any guild stays together in the long run is mutual respect and helping one another. <br /><br />In the past several months, the atmoshpere has changed. The goal of TIME is the one and only guiding light and those that can&#039;t keep up or want to explore the rest of the game seem to have become the targets of a growing sense of aspersion and disrespect. This too saddens me....EQ is a pasttime not a lifestyle. Hege used to be a warm and welcoming guild where, when logging on, one could count on cries of HI from most online at the time. Now, it seems greeting those logging on is an infrequent occurence. While this is certainly a trivial thing, I have come to feel that it is symptomatic of what we have become. &nbsp;<br /><br />I think the goal of Time can be obtained without Hege abandoning its old feel and pespective on members and apps. We can help one another catch up and still move forward as a guild. However, this is going to require that all of us reestablish a desire to help one another and not disparage each other for having less time to play, a desire to seek and explore what else the game offers, or whatever may divert our attention from the single-minded goal of entering Time. <br /><br />I realize this is not my best writing, but it is coming from my heart. It&#039;s intention is not to pick at or on anyone or any group. It is, however, intended to say that it is not only the &quot;new apps&quot; feeling gilted and that some of us long-term members may no longer feel we have a place in Hege. <br /><br />Flame me if you like...JMHO <br /><br /><br />Oneiron &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />brildaen<br />Guild Member<br /><br />65 Dark Elf Wizard<br />Joined: 14 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 99<br />Location: Utah<br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 1:30 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />HEHE <br />_________________<br />A wizard is a caster with out mez, we have no ports nor tl&#039;s, nor do we know how to not die, we eat rezes like birthday cake, and we laugh at wood elf warriors. <br /><br />Last edited by brildaen on Sun Apr 04, 2004 2:17 pm; edited 1 time in total <br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Bigtoxic<br />Guild Member<br /><br />65 Troll Warrior<br />Joined: 21 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 90<br /><br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 1:31 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />Let me start off by saying that what im about to say is in no way in reference to the above posts for i havent a clue about that kinda stuff. <br /><br />But....ive always have and always will think that the officers need to step up and make tougher decisions. Dyaan earned my utmost respect the night she booted Zipity for those actions. Asking Heggs to leave because he only chose to raid on the mobs that he needed flags for was another good call. But these have been few and far between. Cutting dead weight is a part of life....and while this is a game its also a part of our lives. <br /><br />And no, i dont believe that having the officer tag gives you the right to boot peope at will but i think steps should be taken. <br /><br />But again these are just my opinions ..your milage may and most likely will vary :)~ <br /><br />Last edited by Bigtoxic on Sun Apr 04, 2004 1:35 pm; edited 1 time in total <br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />tylerborne<br />Guild Member<br />&nbsp;<br />65 Human Cleric<br />Joined: 14 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 127<br /><br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 1:31 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />We are killing Gods here, a hey it&#039;s only a game attitude that causes a wipe will certainly piss me off to no end. I&#039;m here for end game content. If I wanted a family atmosphere I&#039;d be in Brews, or Avatars of Coachside. <br />You call officer threatning removal an &quot;asshole.&quot; I say they are stepping up to the plate. And before you go off deep end, you made your point, now I&#039;m going to try and make mine. You may not want to get to Time, but I do. We are 3 God kills from it now. Xeg is soon to die as well. But for her to die, we don&#039;t need clerics to be in the habbit of saying skip me when it&#039;s their turn to heal. If that doesn&#039;t make sense to you think of it this way. Xegony hits for 2250 quadding. Her AE 1K DD, Mana increase to spell casts, 200 hp / tick dot that lasts for 1.8 minutes, and slow. It has a neg 400 mod, meaning you wont resist it. CHR is set for 1.5 seconds, and cleric says skip me, now MA has 3 seconds CH wont be landing on him. Gguess what? It could mean a wipe cause in that 3 seconds Xeg could have done 9K Melee and 1K DD. So a cleric saying skip me can be disastrous for the raid. <br />_________________<br />Tylerborne <br />Archon of Hegemony <br /><br />Tylerborne <br />Dedluv &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Halius<br />Guild Member<br />&nbsp;<br />65 High Elf Cleric<br />Joined: 15 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 86<br />Location: South Carolina<br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 1:48 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />Hey Tyler how many clerics skip but just don&#039;t say skip? I mean i at least said it. I guess from now on i won&#039;t say skip if i ever get in a position like that again. And some people take this fucking game way to serious. <br />_________________<br />&nbsp; <br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Dyaan<br />Guild Commander<br />&nbsp;<br />65 High Elf Cleric<br />Joined: 11 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 265<br />Location: North Carolina<br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 2:14 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />Quote: <br />tells you, &#039;formal bitch for seeing a freaking SKIP on a god mob. i cant tell u how ticked that made me &#039; <br /><br /><br />Quote: <br />&#039;Halius guildremove him honestly done it way too many times... its why fig dropped&#039; <br />[Sat Apr 03 21:54:58 2004] <br /><br /><br />[Sat Apr 03 21:55:07 2004] You told halius, &#039;why the hell did you skip?&#039; <br />[Sat Apr 03 21:55:18 2004] Halius tells the guild, &#039;where is Essence of Fire?&#039; <br />[Sat Apr 03 21:55:24 2004] Halius tells freak:3, &#039;CH { Tunetwister }&#039; <br />[Sat Apr 03 21:55:38 2004] You told halius, &#039;I need an answer&#039; <br />[Sat Apr 03 21:56:08 2004] Halius tells you, &#039;what?&#039; <br />[Sat Apr 03 21:56:12 2004] You told Halius, &#039;in chr&#039; <br />[Sat Apr 03 21:56:42 2004] Halius tells you, &#039;oh i got dotted and was at 20&amp;PCT; hp so i cured and healed, was a mistake i know&#039; <br />[Sat Apr 03 21:56:49 2004] You told Halius, &#039;major&#039; <br />[Sat Apr 03 21:56:55 2004] You told Halius, &#039;you wre told NEVER skip&#039; <br />[Sat Apr 03 21:57:18 2004] Halius says, &#039;Hail, Essence of Fire&#039; <br />[Sat Apr 03 21:59:53 2004] You told halius, &#039;your skip cause Fig to die&#039; <br />[Sat Apr 03 22:00:01 2004] Halius tells you, &#039;ok i got it thanks&#039; <br />[Sat Apr 03 22:00:18 2004] You told halius, &#039;you should have told a shmmy for RGC...THANKS? you are so wrong&#039; <br />[Sat Apr 03 22:00:44 2004] Halius tells you, &#039;omg its a game, and we killed him for gods sake&#039; <br />[Sat Apr 03 22:00:55 2004] You told Halius, &#039;omg we got lucky and you&#039;ve screwed it up before&#039; <br />[Sat Apr 03 22:01:06 2004] You told Halius, &#039;and we are not having it, you either get it right or get gone&#039; <br />[Sat Apr 03 22:01:18 2004] Halius tells you, &#039;i&#039;m sorry i&#039;m not as perfect as you Dyaan&#039; <br />[Sat Apr 03 22:01:59 2004] Halius tells hegchr:4, &#039;sorry i skiped in the CHR, was my bad, extremely sorry guys&#039; <br />[Sat Apr 03 22:03:42 2004] Halius tells hegchr:4, &#039;i got dotted and was at 20&amp;PCT; health so i cured myself and healed so said skip without thinking and yeah&#039; <br />[Sat Apr 03 22:11:15 2004] Halius tells hegchr:4, &#039;i just want to say sorry again about skipping, won&#039;t happen again and i&#039;m sorry it happened&#039; <br />_________________<br />Dyaan Truesite <br />Archon of Hegemony <br />Recruitment Officer &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Gamehenge<br />Guild Member<br />&nbsp;<br />65 Iksar Shaman<br />Joined: 12 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 81<br />Location: california<br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 2:21 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />I am not taking a side here I&#039;m just trying to state facts. <br /><br />i dont care wich way look at it, we ALL make mistakes. Our pullers, wich are some of the best on the server imo, have messed up pulls and have caused wipes. Should they leave Hegemony? What would Hegemony be without Daark or Loli? You see there seems to be 2 sides in this guild, one wants a friendly atmosphere, and one wants to be end game. I say we can have BOTH. To think we cannot be friendly to each other and respect everyone despite weaknesses but yet still progress is to be, well, ignorant. <br /><br />You can rule a kingdom with fear, people react to fear and stay in line. You can also rule a kingdom with love, people stay in line out of sheer respect. You do NOT respect those you fear. Like I say both work but... <br /><br />here is the clincher <br /><br />If Hegemony decides to make a clear cut decision on wich path it will take, be it love or fear, it will be the end of Hegemony. If that happens I will never play this game again &nbsp;SO lets just keep goign if you actually think we aren&#039;t going to make it into time, well your a freakin pessimist and I can&#039;t help you there. <br /><br />now for my opinion: I think our leaders are the shit and I respect the hell out of them! No, I don&#039;t fear them, i mean, Loli is a chick! ROFL! I think we have many strong players with the drive to beat PoP. But umm Time isnt the end here, this game is ENDLESS and so is existence so why have a time frame? Who cares when we get to Time? Do you actually think fun will improve? Fun is Fun if it isnt fun than it sucks, why the hell would you play a game that sucks? If you are unhappy because your not in &quot;Time&quot; go read a book or get some sunshine, because Time wont be shit after we farmed it for 6 monthes, and youll be crying cause we not in GoD yet. And then I will bump all your posts whining about &quot;not being in Time, Time ASAP! my life will be complete when im in Time! If I could bang Time I would! Time is my whole reason for living! If we arent in Time by next month im going to kill myself!&quot; Just kick back and nuke, slow, heal, tank, mez, pull, buff, whatever the hell your job is, do it to the best of your ability and we will be in Time. Get all huffy and puffy about it and people will start leaving and guild will fall apart. <br />/rant off <br /><br />man i hate getting serious heh <br />_________________<br />Elder Gamehenge <br /><br />&quot;Music is the BEST!&quot; <br />-Frank Zappa &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />bladestep<br />Guild Member<br />&nbsp;<br />65 Dark Elf Rogue<br />Joined: 15 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 137<br /><br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 2:26 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />---------- <br />You told Halius, &#039;and we are not having it, you either get it right or get gone&#039; <br />----------- <br /><br />good thing thats only being applied (unfairly) to Hal. Of course i understand you couldnt make it a blanket rule across the guild, because you you&#039;d end up without a guild. <br /><br />&quot;get it right or get gone&quot;....not sure whats sadder, that that was actually said to someone after an admitted mistake, or that the fact it was said at all is no longer surprising. <br />_________________<br />I speak before I think, therefore I am. <br /><br />I got a fever and the only prescription is more COW BELL! <br /><br />Noli nothis permittere te terere. &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Gamehenge<br />Guild Member<br />&nbsp;<br />65 Iksar Shaman<br />Joined: 12 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 81<br />Location: california<br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 2:30 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />this post applies to this topic <br />_________________<br />Elder Gamehenge <br /><br />&quot;Music is the BEST!&quot; <br />-Frank Zappa &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Nivlack<br />Guild Member<br />&nbsp;<br />65 High Elf Magician<br />Joined: 15 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 4<br /><br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 2:38 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />I&#039;m alittle disapointed in how Hal was told if he does something like that again he will be kicked. Dyaan, Daark, Loli and everyone else in the guild have made all of the above mistakes at some time in there EQ career. How many times has Daark or Loli Wiped a raid or pulled without much notice??? I can name a few times ok maybe more then a few. But you don&#039;t see us judging them for it. SHIT HAPPENS. Nothing I repeat NOTHING in this lifetime will be Like the movie &quot; Plesentville&quot; The more people you have the more problems you have to deal with!!! Thats LIFE <br /><br />I can name a few times Morainne has been Threatened by a certine Cleric. You know who I&#039;m talking about. If you force her to leave you will lose alot of people I can be sure of that! HAVE ALITTLE RESPECT &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Darcc<br />Guild Member<br />&nbsp;<br />65 Iksar Monk<br />Joined: 12 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 79<br /><br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 2:47 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />Yes people make mistakes...yadda yadda.....But don&#039;t be so quick to go off on our officers thinking they are the equivalent to a nazi takeover. <br /><br />Questions to ask.. <br /><br />1. Is it a common occurance with this player? <br />2. Was it an easily avoidable mistake? <br /><br />Mistakes will happen....they question is will they happen more often than not. Dragging conversations like this into some Family guild vs Raiding guild arguement is pointless. Ofcourse many people in this guild care about each other as the equivalent of family, but you didnt get where you are today with group hugs and Sunday dinner. You are in a RAIDING guild.....the family atmosphere is player option....YOUR CHOICE. <br /><br />The only reason shit like this gets blown out of poportion is the lack of die hard facts. People are filling in the blanks, and you don&#039;t really know whats happening......stop it. <br /><br />Let me give you an example of one of my BIG mistakes. We were raiding Fire and I had just logged in for the first time in 2 weeks, so I&#039;m a bit...off. <br /><br />/Monk tells you; Oh good your here, you can pull... <br /><br />&#039;Ummm..okay&#039; <br /><br />Roinin tells you: Go get Blazzax... <br />You tell Roinin: But Magmaton is in the way... <br />Roinin Tells you: we need Blazzax First... <br /><br />Off I run for the warping Blazzax....Death hits me 3-400 times..bla bla bla.. <br /><br />Confusion sets in, Loli logs on, Monks are talking strategy in the monk channel, raid is sitting on its thumb.....Someone says: We need to get Magmaton out of the way. <br /><br />I thought Loli said that......I ask if we are ready for the pull...no reponse <br /><br />Bla bla bla <br /><br />I pull Magmaton.....I die on the ramp before he hits camp, but the others do their job...Ranger WS&#039;s him in, Tank steps up.....Clerics arent ready for Magmaton healing, we win.....with about 15 of 70 people left standing. <br /><br />I get some tells from officers.....I know I screwed up, but I&#039;m not really looking what the officer&#039;s are saying. I&#039;m looking at the fact that I just probably wasted an hour of all my guilds time.... 70 people that I caused a set-back too due to some basic confusion. <br /><br />Do I take this game ultra-seriously? No. Do I respect all the people I share this game with? Your damn right I do!! Realize that when you make a mistake your not only effecting you.....you effect everyone. Try not to fall into the heated debates of what officers are saying, just make the adjustments and move on with life. Your guild is counting on you &nbsp;<br /><br />Learn from your mistakes, and rise beyond the boundaries of the common player....that will lead you anywhere you want to go. <br />_________________<br />Sensei Darcc ~ Specialist in the Cybering of rocks. <br />&#039;But Sensei Darcc,&#039; The young monk asks, &#039;Why do you Cyber rocks?&#039; <br />&#039;Be warned my young swiftail...EQ transvestites roam the many lands of this realm now, and can strike at anytime. Love thy rocks, for rocks shall always be rocks.&#039; &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Roinin<br />Guild Officer<br /><br />65 Human Magician<br />Joined: 27 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 80<br />Location: Salt Lake City<br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 3:04 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />Before we play the &quot;poor oppressed and down trodden soul&quot; syndrom, this &quot;skip&quot; thing has been going on for quite some time. Halius has been told to never &quot;skip&quot; again numerous times and has fallen on deaf ears each time. <br />The typical repsonce has always been &quot;ok, I&#039;ve got it&quot;, or &quot;don&#039;t worry, it&#039;s under control&quot;. But seeing as it&#039;s an ongoing problem , its indeed not &quot;under control&quot;, as stated. <br /><br />Halius has caused 2 seperate wipes on the Chr team directly attributed to this &quot;skipping&quot; practice. Now, I&#039;m sure you all will agree after being warned multiple times and causing 2 seperate wipes, or near wipes, that something has to change one way or the other. This isnt like 1 or 2 seperate events like being portrayed here. It&#039;s just that the two most notable have caused drastic effects on the raid&#039;s outcome. This is an ongoing occurance, despite being asked, begged, or verbally repremanded to stop doing it. <br /><br />I think the point has been made however. But I do wanted to commend your courage to apologize to the guild for the mistakes. And yes, we all make mistakes. I&#039;ve never had to be on CHR, but I understand it to be one of the most stressful areas of our raids. It has to be &quot;on&quot; or the raid as a whole suffers. There is also alot riding on the shoulders of our clerics to get it done, and done right the first time.. Luckily we&#039;ve had a solid group of clerics to work with, and hope it continues as such. <br />_________________<br />Sage Roinin Unsleep <br />65th Arch Convoker <br />Hegemony Rodcet Nife &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Gamehenge<br />Guild Member<br />&nbsp;<br />65 Iksar Shaman<br />Joined: 12 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 81<br />Location: california<br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 3:07 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />a few people are coming down on Dyaan atm, and in her defence, In a year and a half of raiding/grinding with her I have NEVER seen her make a mistake, so yes maybe she is qualified to shake her finger at Halius. <br />_________________<br />Elder Gamehenge <br /><br />&quot;Music is the BEST!&quot; <br />-Frank Zappa &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Aislynne<br />Guild Member<br />&nbsp;<br />65 Wood Elf Druid<br />Joined: 15 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 52<br /><br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 3:14 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: Halius &nbsp; <br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />Thts true Darcc. However you do realize it was a mistake and we all do. We all at one time or another have made mistakes in game that cause a wipe or some sort or another. We are only human and we make mistakes. And there has often been times when I had to choose wether or not to cure/heal myself or continue healing grp or MT/RT. Its another case of half empty/ half full. And tanks have run out of range all the time hell they push the mob oor 90% of the time lately. But thats the way it goes. Me personally think it was better for him to be alive then dead but again a judgment call. Dont feel bad Hal its an honest mistake and we all make them. No one is excused from that..... <br />_________________<br /><br />Aislynne Voltaire <br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Cenewulfe<br />Guild Member<br /><br />65 Wood Elf Ranger<br />Joined: 16 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 84<br />Location: You haven&#039;t heard of it, Canada<br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 3:27 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />Mistakes, we all make them. Continued bad playing that has caused wipes on multiple raids, find a new guild. <br /><br />Cenewulfe <br />_________________<br />&quot; it not that it wasn&#039;t done well, but one is suprised to find it done at all &quot; &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />zaphe<br />Guild Member<br /><br />65 Iksar Shaman<br />Joined: 13 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 49<br /><br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 3:30 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />Don&#039;t get me wrong .. I have the utmost respect for our officers ... but I also beleive that there are other ways to handle situations than those that I see handled. <br /><br />Tellinga member to step up or step out of a raiding guild is one thing .. telling a member that has appologised and had a *legitimate reason* to get better now or get out (verified by logs) is just plain wrong. Halius isn&#039;t a founder of Hegemony, but he&#039;s a member just as much as I, dyaan, Idnew and even daarksun. <br /><br />Making mistakes is human .. even if you make many mistakes .. even ofthe same kind. Serepi .. you die to incoming mobs 2-3 times more than I have ever or ever will ... is that a mistake on your part? Do you slow or debuff to early .. that can cause ping ponging ... It might wipe a raid ... (not picking on serepi, its just an example that shows situations where things happen on raid .. I love serepi &nbsp;<br /><br />Pulling PoAir at ZI with 6 or 7 Castllians ... that is wipeable but I see us close to wipe at least every other time we attempt PoAir .. that definitely causes down time ever single time we raid ther e.. but it still happens .. continuously .. without fail ... <br /><br />All I&#039;m trying to point out is ... Actions taken by officers need to be thought out *Extremely* well before they are ever put into words. Tellign someone off for doing something stupid is one thing .. telling them off for making a mistake, even if somewhat repeatedly is different. Harping on the issue and continually beatingthem down for it is even worse. Pick an executioner and let them do the talking .. we don&#039;t need all 5 or whatever officers berating people for mistakes we ALL make. <br /><br />EDIT: If Halius is questionable .. put him on spam heals ... I didn&#039;t know that everythign was so black and white lately with the guild. Either he&#039;s CHR or he&#039;s out .. I&#039;ve seen clerics put onspam for not being able to keep up with CHR or don&#039;t have it fine tuned yet .. perhaps theres a better way to approach a problem than with swords drawn. <br />_________________<br />Zaphe Vo`Lok <br />65 Prophet of Cazic-Thule <br />No longer Shaman Class Leader <br />Hegemony, Rodcet Nife Server &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />BevarinRN<br />Guild Member<br />&nbsp;<br />65 Half Elf Ranger<br />Joined: 25 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 51<br /><br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 5:46 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />Heh i made a mistake last night on Hydrotha and it did wipe the raid.. Am i going to get booted? I havent been here that long plus i havent logged in since the wipe was i deguilded while offline ... Noone and i mean noone plays this game perfectly every day... How many times has Halius got it right??? what kind of ratio are you talking about he scew up one in three or one in five or one in thirty ??? I think everyone needs to set back calm down and play the damn &quot; GAME &quot;! <br />_________________<br />Bevarin Taulmaril <br />65 Forest Stalker &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Dulvarian<br />Guild Member<br /><br />65 Half Elf Bard<br />Joined: 12 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 37<br />Location: EST<br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 7:22 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />Lol, joo keeled da bards bev...bad ranja... &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Retrievil<br />Guild Member<br />&nbsp;<br />65 Iksar Necromancer<br />Joined: 13 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 49<br />Location: Canada<br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 7:53 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />Quote: <br />Before we play the &quot;poor oppressed and down trodden soul&quot; syndrom, this &quot;skip&quot; thing has been going on for quite some time. Halius has been told to never &quot;skip&quot; again numerous times and has fallen on deaf ears each time. <br />The typical repsonce has always been &quot;ok, I&#039;ve got it&quot;, or &quot;don&#039;t worry, it&#039;s under control&quot;. But seeing as it&#039;s an ongoing problem , its indeed not &quot;under control&quot;, as stated. <br /><br />Halius has caused 2 seperate wipes on the Chr team directly attributed to this &quot;skipping&quot; practice. Now, I&#039;m sure you all will agree after being warned multiple times and causing 2 seperate wipes, or near wipes, that something has to change one way or the other. This isnt like 1 or 2 seperate events like being portrayed here. It&#039;s just that the two most notable have caused drastic effects on the raid&#039;s outcome. This is an ongoing occurance, despite being asked, begged, or verbally repremanded to stop doing it. &nbsp;<br /><br /><br />Just so you all can read that again. I think that is probably the only salient point in this entire thread. No offense Halius, I do like grouping with you and have never had a problem with you, but if what Roi is saying is true then I have zero sympathy. <br /><br />Certainly if I was told never to do something, as it may cause a wipe, no matter what it was, I would not being doing it, and you would only have to tell me once. <br /><br />None of our officers have ever booted anyone out without EXTREME provocation. Far more than I would tolerate if I was an officer. I have a very hard time believing that Dy or Roi would go off on anyone without a good cause, as I say I&#039;ve seen them eat a lot of shit in the time I&#039;ve been Hege and they usually don&#039;t say anything until its choking them. <br /><br />Unfortunately those clerics who are part of the CH chain are going to be under a lot more pressure to play by the book than those who do other things at raids. You can have the best tank, the most dps, excellent CC, but all it takes is a breakdown of the CHC to wipe everyone. This is just the way the game is unfortunately. <br />_________________<br /><br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />zaphe<br />Guild Member<br /><br />65 Iksar Shaman<br />Joined: 13 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 49<br /><br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 8:18 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />Quote: <br />Unfortunately those clerics who are part of the CH chain are going to be under a lot more pressure to play by the book than those who do other things at raids. You can have the best tank, the most dps, excellent CC, but all it takes is a breakdown of the CHC to wipe everyone. This is just the way the game is unfortunately. &nbsp;<br /><br /><br />And threats, while possibly meant with the utmost constructive criticism, do not help take the stress out of doing your job, they only add to it. <br />_________________<br />Zaphe Vo`Lok <br />65 Prophet of Cazic-Thule <br />No longer Shaman Class Leader <br />Hegemony, Rodcet Nife Server &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Nivlack<br />Guild Member<br />&nbsp;<br />65 High Elf Magician<br />Joined: 15 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 4<br /><br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 8:20 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />I&#039;m so glad I don&#039;t have to deal with any Belitteling in the /hegmage channel I think were all above that. If a mistake is made it&#039;s discused in a Professional manner. not that many of us make mistakes often but we all do at some points. &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Halius<br />Guild Member<br />&nbsp;<br />65 High Elf Cleric<br />Joined: 15 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 86<br />Location: South Carolina<br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 8:29 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />Roinin, whoever is telling you that i have been warned multiple times to not &quot;skip&quot; is either lying or are incorrect. I know that i wasn&#039;t suppose to skip and i knew that right after i did it. As i said in my post above. I have never been sent a tell by an officer saying don&#039;t skip or anyone in that matter. I also can&#039;t remember 2 raids i have wiped, i have almost wiped a FR raid and thats it. The Xegony raid when i said skip (remember i was casting but the MT was OOR), we were on our 2nd or 3rd MT and the raid was falling apart anyway so it wasn&#039;t my fault. We all make mistakes but cleric&#039;s (and a few other classes) mistakes are just put under a microscope. <br />_________________<br />&nbsp; <br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Binthaf<br />Guild Member<br /><br />65 Dwarf Cleric<br />Joined: 15 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 106<br /><br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 8:38 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />This is the only guild i have ever been in that didn&#039;t put its cleric &quot;A&quot; team in the CHR. We typically have 1 or 2 clerics that have no business (mana, ability to count, what ever) in the rotation. <br /><br />I don&#039;t know about any past problems with Halius, but last night I told dyaan we needed to set up cleric groups so we could get healed when we got AE&#039;d. I was told we would avoid the ae and not have a problem. If placement is: fig mob clerics...then at max range i&#039;m gonna need a far sight of luck to avoid the AE the whole fight and still hit fig with cheal. <br /><br />should he have ducked out, no. <br /><br />I don&#039;t see our pet classes getting booted over push (time after time after time) <br /><br />I don&#039;t see tanks getting booted for failing to pick up adds (time after time after time). <br /><br />I don&#039;t see 2/3 of the melee getting booted for pushing mobs all over the freaking zone or walling them and not stopping (time after time after time) <br /><br />Lets take the 5-10 people that the raid rides on (yep the chr is the most important part of the raid) and threaten them. <br /><br />Or maybe, like other guilds, our chr should be the &quot;A&quot; team of the clerics. <br /><br />#1 slot your biggest baddest cleric online <br />#2-#Y alternate strong mana to weak mana <br />#last- Your second biggest baddest cleric online. <br /><br />Never ask someone to do something your not willing to do yourself &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Retrievil<br />Guild Member<br />&nbsp;<br />65 Iksar Necromancer<br />Joined: 13 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 49<br />Location: Canada<br />&nbsp;Posted: Sun Apr 04, 2004 11:58 pm &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />For the record, I&#039;m all for booting repeat offenders of any class. <br /><br />I&#039;m not talking about mistakes here. I would never bitch someone out for making an honest error, even if it happened more than once. Hell as people say how many times has Daark wiped us? I seem to remember quite a few Daarksun tells Hegraid: Oops. and then a pack of mobs from hell shortly after. I seem to remember myself running directly into a room full of mobs our last VT trip. Those are mistakes. <br /><br />That is quite different than being asked specifically not to do something, like dont assist until called, or don&#039;t have pets, or whatever, and then the person continues to do it. <br /><br />I&#039;m not saying you did anything like that Halius, just clarifying what I mean when I said I dont have any sympathy. &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Serepi Serein<br />Guild Officer / Treasurer<br />&nbsp;<br />65 Iksar Shaman<br />Joined: 11 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 237<br />Location: South Dakota!<br />&nbsp;Posted: Mon Apr 05, 2004 7:07 am &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />zaphe wrote: <br />I love serepi &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br /><br /><br />This post will be an example of the ostrich response. I&#039;ll ignore everything else, and just read/hear what I want to read~! <br /><br />I love you too! <br />_________________<br /><br />Serepi Serein<br />Officer, Hegemony Guild<br /><br />&quot;You see, loneliness is the price we pay for being born in this modern age, so full of freedom, independence and our own egotistical selves.&quot; -- Natsume Soseki, Kokoro, 1914. &nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Back to top &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />Hunters<br />Guild Member<br />&nbsp;<br />65 Wood Elf Ranger<br />Joined: 15 Feb 2004<br />Posts: 172<br /><br />&nbsp;Posted: Mon Apr 05, 2004 8:29 am &nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: &nbsp; &nbsp;<br /><br />--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />&nbsp;<br />The number of times that anyone has been threatened with deguilding or has actually been deguilded is extremely small. This goes to show you that if the action is being threatened then it is likely not over one occurrence or three or five. It is very likely due to more than just the event in question and a reflection of overall performance. Those of you that are quick to judge the officers need to realize you don’t have all the information they do. <br /><br />Family guild: <br />Anyone that thinks this is a family guild just because that is where we came from is not facing facts. We are a raiding guild. We are different from some other raiding guilds in that we have more respect our fellow members and we don’t often berate people in /gu but that doesn’t make us a family guild, it just makes us different. Different &lt;&gt; “family guild” <br />_________________<br />Hunter Hunters, 65 Ranger / Forest Stalker, Endless Quiver, Archery Mastery III <br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
