							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=751.msg6751#msg6751"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=751.msg6751#msg6751">Re:Good guild going bad</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #4 on:</b> April 06, 2004, 02:11:04 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">I think the goal of Time can be obtained without Hege abandoning its old feel and pespective on members and apps<br /></div><br />This is very true.. when Warlords of Wrath ( A family guild ) and Anthology ( A raiding guild ) first merged, a lot of discussion was out an about on the subject of Casual VS Hardcore. &nbsp;our goals at the time were elemental.. but we eventually got time (#3!) etc etc.. &nbsp;We still have a core WoW folk (some casual some hardcore), and a core Anthology (same).. <br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
