							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=751.msg6753#msg6753"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=751.msg6753#msg6753">Re:Good guild going bad</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #6 on:</b> April 06, 2004, 02:25:32 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Ok last comment for now<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">The number of times that anyone has been threatened with deguilding or has actually been deguilded is extremely small. This goes to show you that if the action is being threatened then it is likely not over one occurrence or three or five. It is very likely due to more than just the event in question and a reflection of overall performance. Those of you that are quick to judge the officers need to realize you don’t have all the information they do. <br /></div><br />While they may not go through with the threats.. that causes MANY problems..<br /><br />* It gives the members a belief that officers won&#039;t go through with what they say (whether it is a Guild Vision Plan, Disciplinary Actions, whatnot).. They lose credibility in otherwords<br /><br />* It may make some people think they can get away with anything and cause problems.. (Drama, whatnot)<br /><br />* MOST IMPORTANTLY.. It demorilizes people. &nbsp;Do you really want to tell someone they could get kicked?? They may quit or go casual, or leave for another guild! &nbsp;A simple scold &quot;You should not have skipped.. Please know this for future reference..&quot; Would have been suffice.. <br /><br />Everyone makes mistakes (even officers), and not talking about raid content.. Halis you should really try talking with the officers of hegemony in a channel and work through this.. &nbsp;If the officers are unwilling or unappreciative of your effort to set things straight.. perhaps you are in the wrong guild
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
