								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Does AOL dialup still assign you a new IP address every time you log on? &nbsp;They use to. &nbsp;So all you need is an AOL username. &nbsp;Use a relative&#039;s account or something (don&#039;t admit to having AOL yourself!). &nbsp;Now use dialup to log in instead of your broadband connection. &nbsp;Make an account. &nbsp;Have fun. &nbsp;<br /><br />(Disclaimer: This post should not be construed to support anon flaming in any way. &nbsp;Information in this post should not be used to perpetrate anon flaming. &nbsp;The poster will not be held liable for any and all past or future anon flames on this or other boards.)
						</td>
